  @base = http://127.0.0.1:5050

### 1. Register (code appears in the cmd window)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test@atu.ie", "password": "password123" }

### 2. Login before verifying -> expect 403
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test@atu.ie", "password": "password123" }

### 3. Verify (paste the code from the terminal)
POST {{base}}/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test@atu.ie", "code": "123006" }

### 4. Login -> expect 200 and a token
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test@atu.ie", "password": "password123" }

### 5. Who am I? (uses the token from request 4)
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 6. No token -> expect 401
GET {{base}}/auth/me